/postalloc-scheduling-baseline/
/bench/evidence/
/.cpcache/
/.clj-kondo/.cache/
/target/
/node_modules/
# ...and node_modules as a SYMLINK, which the trailing slash above does not
# match. That is how one got committed on 2026-09-06 (25591e0a): it pointed at
# its own absolute path, so `npx --no-install nbb` -- bin/kotoba's shebang --
# died with ELOOP in any checkout at that path and the CLI would not start.
/node_modules
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/.tools/
*.kexe
*.kexe.provenance.edn
*.kexe.publication.edn
*.wasm
# Golden fixtures for test/nbb/run.cljs are checked in on purpose (the
# nbb-native wasm32 path's byte-identical cross-check against the JVM
# path needs them committed, not regenerated on every clone).
!test/nbb/golden/*.wasm
test/nbb/golden/*.wasm.provenance.edn

# Bench/falsify tick scratch under docs/. docs/ is a prose directory: it tracks
# 325 .md and 60 .edn and zero files of any extension below.
/docs/*.py
/docs/*.sh
/docs/*.txt
/docs/*.log
/docs/*.status
/docs/*.size
/docs/*.bak*

# .nbb/ is deliberately NOT ignored here, and the cache under it is deliberately
# committed. nbb builds `nbb-deps.jar` by shelling out to babashka, and the
# GitHub-hosted runners this repo's jobs use do not have `bb` -- this workspace
# retired it as a script host (ADR-2607173000). The committed cache is what
# stands in for it. Measured 2026-09-10: removing those eight files turned
# `server-kind` from success (88s) into failure in 15s with `/bin/sh: 1: bb: not
# found`, from `bb --config .nbb/.cache/<hash>/deps.edn ... uberjar`. The <hash>
# is over the resolved dependency set, so a new one is needed whenever deps.edn
# moves -- an ignore rule here would break CI again at the next dependency bump.
